AC97: keep codec volume across voice reopen.

open_voice() reopens the PCM voices when the guest changes the sample rate,
and the audio layer resets a reopened voice to nominal volume. The codec
Master and PCM Out (and Record Gain) settings were not reapplied, so a
Windows XP guest could not change or mute the master volume: the next sound
at a different rate played at full volume again. Reapply them after opening.

--- ./hw/audio/ac97.c
+++ ./hw/audio/ac97.c
@@ -306,6 +306,9 @@
     return val;
 }
 
+static void update_combined_volume_out(AC97LinkState *s);
+static void update_volume_in(AC97LinkState *s);
+
 static void open_voice(AC97LinkState *s, int index, int freq)
 {
     struct audsettings as;
@@ -327,6 +330,8 @@
                 pi_callback,
                 &as
                 );
+            /* A reopened voice starts at nominal volume. */
+            update_volume_in(s);
             break;
 
         case PO_INDEX:
@@ -338,6 +343,13 @@
                 po_callback,
                 &as
                 );
+            /*
+             * Reopening the voice for a new sample rate resets it to nominal
+             * volume, so reapply the codec's Master and PCM Out settings;
+             * otherwise the guest's master volume and mute were lost at the
+             * next stream with a different rate.
+             */
+            update_combined_volume_out(s);
             break;
 
         case MC_INDEX:
